{"parentUuid":"73026747-32cd-477a-96e2-a4322f7d418b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YTseDpMkYyiAKAMiEV3RDw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015KD4hxuGGhpupyPCBMBwo6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\prime_silo_togaf_report_manifest_fixes.md","content":"---\nname: prime_silo_togaf_report_manifest_fixes\ndescription: TOGAF report swarm — fixed manifest var-substitution (267MB explosion + ${model} not resolved); local model wedge diagnosis\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n2026-06-30: Investigated why TOGAF SAD report generation took 38 min and failed. Found and fixed two distinct bugs in `prime-silo/runtime`, both in report-swarm manifest handling. Relates to [[project_prime_silo_offload_orchestrator]] and [[project_bridge_4k_studio_observability]].\n\n**Bug 1 — running the manifest (`${model}` never resolved).** Report-swarm templates (schema_version 2.0, e.g. `manifests/templates/togaf_sad_report_swarm.json`) carry a `variables` block and reference it via `${model}`/`${topic}`/`${output_file}`. `SwarmManifest` (core/manifest.py) has no `variables` field (Pydantic silently drops it) and `_load_manifest` in `benny_cli.py` validated raw JSON with no substitution → literal `\"${model}\"` reached litellm → every task failed instantly with \"LLM Provider NOT provided\" (run-7ee9b7167d01, 08:58). Fix: added `_render_manifest_vars()` (bounded per-token str.replace, max 4 passes, fixpoint break) called in `_load_manifest`; `cmd_run` passes `--model`/`--workspace` overrides and fails-fast if a `${` token survives in `config.model`. Added `--model` flag to `run` subparser + top-level `import os`.\n\n**Bug 2 — generating the manifest (267MB combinatorial explosion).** `manifests/togaf_sad_prime_silo.json` was 267 MB of degenerate `output_file × topic × model` interleave (a recursive/char-level substitution gone wrong: `''.join(output_file+c for c in ''.join(topic+c2 for c2 in model))`). Deleted it; regenerated correctly via `_render_manifest_vars` → 9 KB valid 6-task manifest. The new bounded renderer cannot produce this (test covers self-referential vars staying bounded).\n\n**Tests:** `tests/test_manifest_var_substitution.py` (5 pass) — resolution, overrides, validates+small, no-explosion, unresolved-token-left-for-guard.\n\n**Root cause of the 38-min failure:** the request \"Generate a TOGAF-Plus SAD\" was run through the *planner*, which JIT-expanded it into **45 tasks**. The local model `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` runs ~6 tok/s and serializes one request at a time → ~38 min then failed at aggregation. The **6-task template** is the single-laptop path, but was unrunnable until Bug 1 was fixed. Use `benny run manifests/togaf_sad_prime_silo.json` (template), NOT the planner, for this.\n\n**Local model wedge (operational, env state).** Lemonade on **127.0.0.1:13305** (`/api/v1`). `/models` answers in 2ms but generation (`/chat/completions`) hangs even for 8 tokens after the heavy run history + a request killed mid-flight (the FLM/NPU backend doesn't release). It worked early in session (12s/80tok). Recovery = restart LemonadeServer (`LemonadeServer.exe serve --port 13305`). Lesson: killing a swarm run mid-generation can wedge the model server.\n\n**Offload MCP (`prime-silo-nexus__offload_exec`):** operational — async enqueue (`wait:false`) works and writes to `benny-home/workspaces/default/offload/inbox/`; sync (`wait:true`) routes through the same local model so it's blocked while wedged. Acceptance_criteria must be objects `{id:\"ac1\",statement:...}`, risk_tier ∈ green|yellow|red.\n\n**Not fully isolated:** the LangGraph swarm executor (`graph.ainvoke`) showed 0 model calls / 0 governance events for minutes on the template run — but since the model was wedging, couldn't separate an executor stall from slow/wedged generation. Re-check after a clean lemonade restart. Helper added: `scripts/run_report_manifest.py` = direct sequential wave runner (bypasses the swarm executor) for single-laptop report eval.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":175095,"output_tokens":1638,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1638,"cache_read_input_tokens":175095,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":799},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcZHGWjmsP52NgSbmfXHD","attributionMcpServer":"prime-silo-nexus","attributionMcpTool":"offload_exec","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a855916-6cb1-411b-ab18-7b842af456aa","timestamp":"2026-06-30T10:24:47.322Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"24644cca-cf95-422d-a482-74215d3f764e","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
