{"parentUuid":"0c2b6847-5a76-467c-abf5-5c158bcd2661","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GuzAZEowwezDUZaHVeKDs8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The runner is tuned and ready. Here's where things stand.\n\n## What was going wrong\n\n**Two distinct bugs, both in report-swarm manifest handling (`prime-silo/runtime`):**\n\n1. **Running the manifest** — Report-swarm templates use a `variables` block with `${model}` / `${topic}` / `${output_file}` tokens, but `SwarmManifest` has no `variables` field and [`_load_manifest`](prime-silo/runtime/benny_cli.py) validated the raw JSON with **no substitution**. So the literal string `\"${model}\"` reached litellm and every task failed instantly with *\"LLM Provider NOT provided\"* (run `run-7ee9b7167d01`, 08:58).\n\n2. **Generating the manifest** — `manifests/togaf_sad_prime_silo.json` was **267 MB** of degenerate output: a combinatorial explosion where the output path wrapped every char of the topic, which wrapped every char of the model string (`output_file × topic × model`). A recursive/char-level substitution gone wrong.\n\n**Why the report took 38 min and failed:** that run (`run-cfb1949a3605`, \"Generate a TOGAF-Plus SAD\") went through the **planner**, which JIT-expanded the request into **45 tasks**. The local `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` runs ~6 tok/s and serializes one request at a time → ~38 min, then failed at aggregation. The **6-task template** is the single-laptop-optimized path — but it was unrunnable because of bug #1.\n\n## What I fixed (verified)\n\n- Added a **bounded** `_render_manifest_vars()` (per-token `str.replace`, max 4 passes, fixpoint break — structurally cannot explode) applied on manifest load, plus a fail-fast guard in `cmd_run` and a new `--model` override flag.\n- **Deleted the corrupt 267 MB file** and regenerated it correctly → **9 KB**, valid, 6 tasks, model resolved to `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM`.\n- **Verified live:** `benny run` now loads `tasks=6 model=lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` with no `${model}` failure.\n- **Regression tests:** `tests/test_manifest_var_substitution.py` — 5/5 pass (resolution, overrides, validates-and-small, no-explosion-on-self-referential-vars, unresolved-token-left-for-guard).\n- Added `scripts/run_report_manifest.py` — a direct sequential wave runner for single-laptop report eval, now right-sized (700 tok/task, 300s cap).\n\n## Local model + offload MCP\n\n- **Local model:** healthy early (12s for an 80-tok call), confirming `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` works. But its **generation engine is now wedged** — `/models` answers in 2ms, yet `/chat/completions` hangs even for 8 tokens. This set in after the heavy run history + a request being killed mid-flight (the FLM/NPU backend didn't release). Hence your restart.\n- **Offload MCP (`offload_exec`):** operational — async enqueue (`wait:false`) works; sync (`wait:true`) is blocked only because it routes through the same wedged model.\n\n**When you've restarted LemonadeServer, just say \"it's up\"** and I'll run `scripts/run_report_manifest.py manifests/togaf_sad_prime_silo.json`, report the per-task timing, and show the generated TOGAF SAD. I also want to re-check one open item then: on the template run the LangGraph swarm executor showed 0 calls for minutes, but I couldn't separate an executor stall from the wedging model — worth confirming against a fresh model."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":181567,"output_tokens":1256,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1256,"cache_read_input_tokens":181567,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536