-home/workspaces/default/offload/inbox/`; sync (`wait:true`) routes through the same local model so it's blocked while wedged. Acceptance_criteria must be objects `{id:\"ac1\",statement:...}`, risk_tier ∈ green|yellow|red.\n\n**Not fully isolated:** the LangGraph swarm executor (`graph.ainvoke`) showed 0 model calls / 0 governance events for minutes on the template run — but since the model was wedging, couldn't separate an executor stall from slow/wedged generation. Re-check after a clean lemonade restart. Helper added: `scripts/run_report_manifest.py` = direct sequential wave runner (bypasses the swarm executor) for single-laptop report eval.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":21,"oldLines":4,"newStart":21,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **Offload MCP (`prime-silo-nexus__offload_exec`):** operational — async enqueue (`wait:false`) works and writes to `benny-home/workspaces/default/offload/inbox/`; sync (`wait:true`) routes through the same local model so it's blocked while wedged. Acceptance_criteria must be objects `{id:\"ac1\",statement:...}`, risk_tier ∈ green|yellow|red."," ","-**Not fully isolated:** the LangGraph swarm executor (`graph.ainvoke`) showed 0 model calls / 0 governance events for minutes on the template run — but since the model was wedging, couldn't separate an executor stall from slow/wedged generation. Re-check after a clean lemonade restart. Helper added: `scripts/run_report_manifest.py` = direct sequential wave runner (bypasses the swarm executor) for single-laptop report eval.","+**Bug 3 — swarm executor \"stall\" was a hidden 3000-token grind (FIXED).** `benny run` on the template showed 0 `llm_calls.jsonl` entries for minutes and looked hung. Pinpointed via `scratch/diag_swarm_nodes.py` (times each node directly): planner/wave_scheduler/orchestrator are instant; the hang is in `executor_node`. Cause: `executor_node`'s LOCAL-model path (swarm.py ~line 799) does NOT go through `call_model` — it calls `benny/core/local_executor.py`'s `generate()`