{"parentUuid":"99640b69-3776-48d4-a0b6-cbcde6bdeb33","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\prime_silo_togaf_report_manifest_fixes.md","snippet":"1\t---\n2\tname: prime_silo_togaf_report_manifest_fixes\n3\tdescription: \"TOGAF report swarm — fixed manifest var-substitution (267MB explosion + ${model} not resolved); local model wedge diagnosis\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 24644cca-cf95-422d-a482-74215d3f764e\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t2026-06-30: Investigated why TOGAF SAD report generation took 38 min and failed. Found and fixed two distinct bugs in `prime-silo/runtime`, both in report-swarm manifest handling. Relates to [[project_prime_silo_offload_orchestrator]] and [[project_bridge_4k_studio_observability]].\n11\t\n12\t**Bug 1 — running the manifest (`${model}` never resolved).** Report-swarm templates (schema_version 2.0, e.g. `manifests/templates/togaf_sad_report_swarm.json`) carry a `variables` block and reference it via `${model}`/`${topic}`/`${output_file}`. `SwarmManifest` (core/manifest.py) has no `variables` field (Pydantic silently drops it) and `_load_manifest` in `benny_cli.py` validated raw JSON with no substitution → literal `\"${model}\"` reached litellm → every task failed instantly with \"LLM Provider NOT provided\" (run-7ee9b7167d01, 08:58). Fix: added `_render_manifest_vars()` (bounded per-token str.replace, max 4 passes, fixpoint break) called in `_load_manifest`; `cmd_run` passes `--model`/`--workspace` overrides and fails-fast if a `${` token survives in `config.model`. Added `--model` flag to `run` subparser + top-level `import os`.\n13\t\n14\t**Bug 2 — generating the manifest (267MB combinatorial explosion).** `manifests/togaf_sad_prime_silo.json` was 267 MB of degenerate `output_file × topic × model` interleave (a recursive/char-level substitution gone wrong: `''.join(output_file+c for c in ''.join(topic+c2 for c2 in model))`). Deleted it; regenerated correctly via `_render_manifest_vars` → 9 KB valid 6-task manifest. The new bounded renderer cannot produce this (test covers self-referential vars staying bounded).\n15\t\n16\t**Tests:** `tests/test_manifest_var_substitution.py` (5 pass) — resolution, overrides, validates+small, no-explosion, unresolved-token-left-for-guard.\n17\t\n18\t**Root cause of the 38-min failure:** the request \"Generate a TOGAF-Plus SAD\" was run through the *planner*, which JIT-expanded it into **45 tasks**. The local model `lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` runs ~6 tok/s and serializes one request at a time → ~38 min then failed at aggregation. The **6-task template** is the single-laptop path, but was unrunnable until Bug 1 was fixed. Use `benny run manifests/togaf_sad_prime_silo.json` (template), NOT the planner, for this.\n19\t\n20\t**Local model wedge (operational, env state).** Lemonade on **127.0.0.1:13305** (`/api/v1`). `/models` answers in 2ms but generation (`/chat/completions`) hangs even for 8 tokens after the heavy run history + a request killed mid-flight (the FLM/NPU backend doesn't release). It worked early in session (12s/80tok). Recovery = restart LemonadeServer (`LemonadeServer.exe serve --port 13305`). Lesson: killing a swarm run mid-generation can wedge the model server.\n21\t\n22\t**Offload MCP (`prime-silo-nexus__offload_exec`):** operational — async enqueue (`wait:false`) works and writes to `benny-home/workspaces/default/offload/inbox/`; sync (`wait:true`) routes through the same local model so it's blocked while wedged. Acceptance_criteria must be objects `{id:\"ac1\",statement:...}`, risk_tier ∈ green|yellow|red.\n23\t\n24\t**Bug 3 — swarm executor \"stall\" was a hidden 3000-token grind (FIXED).** `benny run` on the template showed 0 `llm_calls.jsonl` entries for minutes and looked hung. Pinpointed via `scratch/diag_swarm_nodes.py` (times each node directly): planner/wave_scheduler/orchestrator are instant; the hang is in `executor_node`. Cause: `executor_node`'s LOCAL-model path (swarm.py ~line 799) does NOT go through `call_model` — it calls `benny/core/local_executor.py`'s `generate()` via raw httpx, so (a) nothing logs to `llm_calls.jsonl` (observability gap) and (b) it requested **max_tokens=3000**. At ~6 tok/s that's ~8 min PER task × 6 ≈ 48 min — the real \"38 min not successful\". local_executor default timeout is 900s (`BENNY_LLM_TIMEOUT`). Fix: capped the local path to `BENNY_EXECUTOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default **1200**), honoring per-task `estimated_tokens` when present. Verified: `executor_node` returns in 110s at cap=300 (was an invisible multi-min grind). NB the cloud/LiteLLM branch below it has dead code after an unconditional `break` (lines ~868+) — pre-existing, untouched.\n25\t\n26\t**Successful eval:** `scripts/run_report_manifest.py` (direct sequential wave runner, bypasses the swarm executor; 700 tok/task, 300s/call cap) produced a 2705-word TOGAF SAD in **8.8 min** (6×~87s) at `home/workspaces/default/data_out/TOGAF_SAD_prime_silo.md`. Caveat: the direct runner does pure generation — it does NOT execute the `query_graph`/`read_file`/`search_kb` skills, so the doc is well-structured TOGAF but GENERIC/ungrounded (invented an Order-to-Cash arch, no Mermaid). For a grounded report use the swarm executor (now that Bug 3 is fixed) — it runs the skills.\n27\t\n28\t**Diagram-render hardening + PDF (2026-06-30 follow-up).** Local-model diagrams broke in the user's viewer. Causes (found via real Mermaid CLI `mmdc`): Mermaid C4 (C4Context/Container/Component) is experimental → fails most viewers; PlantUML needs a 2nd engine; `Class`/`Function` are RESERVED in Mermaid erDiagram (`got 'CLASS'`); parens inside `[node labels]` parse-error; duplicate node IDs; merged/unclosed ``` fences. Fix (all in `runtime/scripts/`):\n29\t- `report_finalize.py` — safety net. `finalize(md)`: normalize_fences() repairs merges; per-block autofix (quote reserved ER entities, strip parens) then VALIDATE each with mmdc; DROP non-portable (C4/PlantUML) + still-invalid blocks, replaced with `> _[diagram omitted …]_` → clean doc guaranteed. `to_pdf()`: mmdc → inline SVG, `markdown` lib → HTML, headless Chrome `--print-to-pdf`.\n30\t- `run_report_manifest.py` — added `DIAGRAM_RULES` to the prompt (Mermaid-only; flowchart/graph/sequence/class/erDiagram; no C4/PlantUML; no parens-in-labels; unique IDs; quote reserved ER names) + calls `finalize()` at end (env `REPORT_FINALIZE`/`REPORT_PDF`, default on).\n31\t- PDF gotcha: puppeteer Chromium (mmdc's, `~/.cache/puppeteer/chrome/win64-148`) crashes \"Invalid file descriptor to ICU data received\" when launched from a Python subprocess (works from a shell); the **Playwright** Chromium (`%LOCALAPPDATA%/ms-playwright/chromium-*`) works → `find_chrome()` prefers it. Needs `pip install markdown`. npx must run from a non-OneDrive cwd + temp `npm_config_cache` (OneDrive → npm \"ECOMPROMISED Lock compromised\").\n32\t- Deliverables in `prime-silo/home/workspaces/default/data_out/`: `TOGAF_Plus_SAD_prime_silo.final.md` + `.final.pdf` (15 diagrams, all mmdc-validated). Helpers kept: `clean_report_diagrams.py`, `clean_report_diagrams_v2.py`, `report_finalize.py`."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e5ee3c9b-b45b-4f00-a0d8-223d970e80d9","timestamp":"2026-06-30T15:45:37.786Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime","sessionId":"24644cca-cf95-422d-a482-74215d3f764e","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
