$BENNY_HOME.\n\nCONTAINERS (C4):\n- Backend API — FastAPI / uvicorn on :8005. ~23 route modules under benny/api/ (rag_routes, graph_routes, manifest_routes, pypes_routes, agentamp_routes, governance_routes, llm_routes, offload_routes, vision_routes, chat_routes, task_routes, system_routes, deep_produce_routes, kg3d). Governance middleware (X-Benny-API-Key) + SSE event bus.\n- Studio UI — React 19 / Vite / Three.js on :3000. Single SPA: Workflow Studio + Notebook (KnowledgeGraphCanvas) + Code Graph (CodeGraphCanvas).\n- Neo4j — :7474 (HTTP) / :7687 (Bolt). DUAL graph in one instance: Code graph (CodeEntity, File, Class, Function; DEFINES/DEPENDS_ON edges) + Knowledge graph (Concept, Document/Source; RELATES_TO/SOURCED_FROM); CORRELATES_WITH edges link the two (enrichment overlay).\n- SQLite run-store — RunRecord history + LangGraph checkpoints.\n\nKEY COMPONENTS / SERVICES:\n- Swarm executor: benny/graph/swarm.py — LangGraph state machine (planner → wave_scheduler → orchestrator → dispatcher → executor → context_handover → expansion_monitor → review → aggregator). Driven by a signed SwarmManifest JSON (plan/DAG/waves). Plan→approve→execute lifecycle with HITL gates.\n- Manifest runner: benny/graph/manifest_runner.py (plan_from_requirement, execute_manifest).\n- LLM router: benny/core/models.py (call_model — offline guard + logging + lineage) and benny/core/local_executor.py (local providers: lemonade :13305, ollama, lmstudio, fastflowlm; OpenAI-compatible).\n- RAG / Knowledge: benny/api/rag_routes.py + benny/core/adaptive_rag.py (Chroma vectors + Neo4j concepts).\n- Code intelligence: benny/graph/code_analyzer.py (Tree-Sitter AST → Neo4j), benny/api/graph_routes.py.\n- Pypes engine: benny/pypes/ — manifest-driven DAG, bronze→silver→gold stages, CLP (Conceptual/Logical/Physical) lineage, checkpoints, drill-down.\n- AgentAmp cockpit: benny/agentamp/ — skinnable .aamp skin packs, HMAC signing.\n- Governance/audit/lineage: benny/governance/ (queued event worker, audit refs).\n- MCP server for Claude: benny/mcp/server.py (prime-silo-nexus: semantic_search, execute_cypher, get_graph_stats, offload_exec).\n- Offload orchestrator: benny/core/offload/ (aamp.offload_task manifests; risk router green/yellow/red; deterministic+judge gate).\n- Portable home: benny/portable/ (init/up/down/status/doctor under $BENNY_HOME).\n\nACTORS/ROLES: Operator/Architect (human, plans & approves manifests), Claude/external agent (via MCP, read-only on deterministic zone; drafts in agent_sandbox), Swarm personas (planner, architect, designer, developer, data_architect, analyst, editor).\n\nDATA ENTITIES: SwarmManifest, ManifestTask, RunRecord, Concept, Source/Document, CodeEntity (File/Class/Function), GovernanceEvent/AuditRef, Workspace.\n\nDEPLOYMENT: single-laptop; Docker services (Neo4j, Marquez, Phoenix, N8N) via docker-compose; desktop app via Electron (Space-Agent shell).\n\nINGESTED STANDARDS available in the knowledge graph (cite where relevant): \"The TOGAF Standard, 10th Edition\", \"uml-models\", \"advanced-data-engineering-with-databricks\".\n\nDIAGRAM RULES: Emit EVERY diagram as a fenced code block. Use ```mermaid for BPMN swimlanes (flowchart), Use-Case, Sequence (sequenceDiagram), Robustness (graph LR with Boundary/Control/Entity), C4 (C4Context/C4Container/C4Component), and ER (erDiagram). Use ```plantuml (@startuml…@enduml) for class skeletons. Diagrams must reference the REAL components above.\n\nADDITIONAL GROUND TRUTH for a comprehensive SAD:\n\nINTERACTION CHANNELS (every way an actor touches the system):\n- Studio UI (React/Three.js :3000): Workflow Studio, Notebook + KnowledgeGraphCanvas (RAG), Studio + CodeGraphCanvas, kg3d/ontology 3D, AgentAmp cockpit, Run History/Lineage, HITL approval gates, Settings/Home-directory config, document drag-drop ingestion, vision-ingestion review.\n- CLI: `benny` (benny_cli.py) — plan/run/runs/enrich/pypes(plan/run/drilldown/rerun/agent-report/bench/chat)/agentamp(scaffold/pack/sign/install/enqueue/export)/up/down/status/doctor/req; `space` (space.js) — registry/memory/serve/version/get/set/help.\n- MCP server (prime-silo-nexus, benny/mcp/server.js + benny/mcp/server.py): semantic_search, execute_cypher, get_graph_stats, find_correlated_concepts, offload_exec. Read-only on the deterministic zone.\n- REST API (FastAPI :8005, ~23 route modules), governed by X-Benny-API-Key; SSE event bus for live updates.\n- A2A (agent-to-agent) protocol: benny/a2a/ (client/server/registry).\n- Desktop system tray (Electron/Space-Agent): configure Home Directory, start/stop services, tray terminal.\n- File ingestion: data_in/staging → promote_staged_files → RAG/vision pipeline.\n\nACTORS: Operator/Architect (human; plans, approves, signs — only humans sign/pin), End-user/Analyst (queries docs, views graphs), Claude/External Agent (via MCP/A2A; read deterministic zone, draft in agent_sandbox), Swarm personas (planner/architect/designer/developer/data_architect/analyst/editor), CI/CD system (GitHub Actions), Admin/Operator (services, home, releases).\n\nNON-FUNCTIONAL: local-first/offline (BENNY_OFFLINE kill-switch); single-laptop performance (model ~6 tok/s, serialized); portability (everything under $BENNY_HOME, no absolute paths — SR-1 gate ≤408 path violations); determinism (ADR-001: deterministic zone read-only for agents, review sandbox for drafts); reproducibility (signed SwarmManifest, content_hash, sha256/hmac signature); privacy (local inference, sensitive_data routing); observability (lineage + events); maintainability (24 route modules, ~200 tests).\n\nSECURITY: ADR-001 determinism boundary; ADR-003 agent-scope credential binding (two proxy facades) + same-origin isolation; HMAC-SHA256 manifest signing (BENNY_HMAC_KEY); X-Benny-API-Key on all API calls (GOVERNANCE_WHITELIST exceptions); governance middleware + audit refs (queued worker, integrity hashes); offline guard (OfflineRefusal); least-skills security (ephemeral manifest per task).\n\nDEVSECOPS / CI-CD: GitHub Actions — release-desktop.yml (builds 6 platforms: Win/macOS/Linux × x64+arm64), snapshot-build.yml (every commit); scripts/manage-release.js (version bump + tag); 6σ release gates run by pytest tests/release: G-COV (≥85% coverage), G-SR1 (≤408 absolute-path violations, tests/portability), G-LAT (<300ms plan latency), G-ERR (0 flakes), G-SIG (manifest signature integrity), G-OFF (offline compliance). Critical: push main before tag or jobs skip.\n\nDEPLOYMENT TOPOLOGIES:\n- Desktop (single-laptop): Electron Space-Agent shell wraps the FastAPI backend; zero-install runtime bundle ships Python+Neo4j+JRE inside the EXE (supervisor + assembler auto-boot); system tray; runtime fetched as a release ASSET. NSIS installer (x64); per-install key.\n- Server-based: docker-compose.yml services — Neo4j (graph), Marquez (OpenLineage), Phoenix (LLM tracing/observability), N8N (automation). FastAPI via uvicorn. Multi-machine model mesh via BENNY_MODEL_ENDPOINTS (endpoint pool → fan-out parallelism in deep_produce / swarm).\n\nOBSERVABILITY: logs/llm_calls.jsonl (per-call model/tokens/duration), governance events (NODE_EXECUTION_STATE) over SSE, Marquez lineage, Phoenix traces, AER (Action-Event-Reasoning) log, run-store SQLite (RunRecord), `benny doctor`/`status` health.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":7,"newStart":29,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," INGESTED STANDARDS available in the knowledge graph (cite where relevant): \"The TOGAF Standard, 10th Edition\", \"uml-models\", \"advanced-data-engineering-with-databricks\"."," ","-DIAGRAM RULES: Emit EVERY diagram as a fenced code block. Use ```mermaid for BPMN swimlanes (flowchart), Use-Case, Sequence (sequenceDiagram), Robustness (graph LR with Boundary/Control/Entity), C4 (C4Context/C4Container/C4Component), and ER (erDiagram). Use ```plantuml (@startuml…@enduml) for class skeletons. Diagrams must reference the REAL components above.","+DIAGRAM RULES: Mermaid ONLY, in ```mermaid blocks. Allowed types: flowchart, graph,